<ServiceHero
  section="services"
  slug="dishwasher-repair/ge-not-draining"
  eyebrow="GE Dishwasher Not Draining · C2 Code · Same Day Southern California"
  title="GE Dishwasher Not Draining: What's Wrong and How to Fix It"
  subtitle="Standing water in a GE dishwasher, or a C2 code, is usually the disposal plug, filter, hose, or pump. Here's the order to check and when to call."
  heroImageTitle="GE Dishwasher Not Draining"
  showBranches={true}
/>

<!-- 01 ANSWER-FIRST -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">01 · The short answer</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">GE dishwasher won't drain? Start at the garbage disposal.</h2>

    <p><strong>Standing water in a GE dishwasher (and the C2 code, which just means the pump-out didn't finish in time) almost always traces to one of four things: a garbage-disposal knockout plug left in after a new disposal install, a clogged filter or drain hose, a blocked sink air gap, or a failed drain pump. The first three are safe to check yourself in a few minutes. The pump is where our techs take over. If your dishwasher stopped draining right after a new disposal went in, that is your answer, the plug. $89 residential diagnostic, waived with repair.</strong></p>

    <p>GE dishwashers share a drain path with the kitchen sink and, in most homes, the garbage disposal. That is why so many "GE won't drain" calls our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair take turn out to be a sink-side blockage rather than a broken dishwasher. Working the problem in the right order saves you a service call more often than not.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 02 CAUSES IN ORDER -->
<section class="section section-gray">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">02 · The causes, in order</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Four causes, most common first.</h2>

    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>1. Disposal knockout plug (new install)</h3>
      <p>New garbage disposals ship with a solid plug sealing the dishwasher drain port. If it wasn't punched out during the install, the dishwasher physically cannot drain. This is the number one cause when a GE stops draining right after disposal or sink work.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>2. Clogged filter or drain hose</h3>
      <p>Food debris, glass grit, and grease collect in the bottom filter and in the drain hose behind the unit. A partial clog slows the drain until the C2 timeout trips; a full clog stops it cold.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>3. Blocked air gap</h3>
      <p>If your sink has an air gap (the small chrome cap on the counter), it can pack with debris and back the water up into the dishwasher. Popping it open and clearing it is a two-minute fix.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>4. Failed drain pump</h3>
      <p>When every path above is clear and water still stands, the drain pump itself has usually failed or its check valve is stuck. This is the one that needs a meter and a replacement part.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 03 SAFE CHECKS -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">03 · What you can safely check</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Five safe steps before you call.</h2>

    <ol class="diag-list">
      <li><strong>Scoop the standing water.</strong> Bail it out with a cup and sponge so you can work and see the filter.</li>
      <li><strong>Run the garbage disposal.</strong> A disposal full of scraps blocks the shared drain. Run it with water for a few seconds and try a rinse cycle.</li>
      <li><strong>Clean the filter.</strong> Twist out the filter at the bottom of the tub, rinse it, and clear any debris in the sump below it.</li>
      <li><strong>Check the drain hose.</strong> Look behind the dishwasher for a kinked or crushed hose, a common issue after the unit has been pushed back into the cabinet.</li>
      <li><strong>Clear the air gap.</strong> If present, pop the chrome cap on the counter and clean out any gunk.</li>
    </ol>

    <p class="callout"><strong>Where to stop:</strong> filter, hose, disposal, and air gap are all safe. Do not remove the drain pump or open the electrical control yourself, and be careful of broken glass in the sump. If water still stands after these steps, it's the pump or the control, and that's our job.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 04 WHEN TO CALL -->
<section class="section section-gray">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">04 · When to call us</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Clear path, still standing water? It's the pump.</h2>

    <p>Once the disposal, filter, hose, and air gap are all verified clear and the tub still holds water (or C2 comes right back), the drain pump or its check valve is the likely fault, and that needs testing and a replacement part. Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair carry the common GE drain pumps, so a confirmed pump failure is usually a one-visit fix. We check the upstream path ourselves first so we never replace a good pump that was fighting a clog, then quote before any work. <strong>$89 residential diagnostic, waived with the repair.</strong> Same-day across <a href="/los-angeles/dishwasher-repair/">Los Angeles</a>, Orange, and Ventura in most cases.</p>

    <p>Related: the general <a href="/services/dishwasher-repair/not-draining/">dishwasher not draining</a> page covers all brands, our <a href="/services/dishwasher-repair/error-codes/">dishwasher error codes</a> guide decodes the rest of GE's codes alongside Bosch, LG, and Samsung, and brand-specific coverage lives on <a href="/brands/ge-dishwasher-repair/">GE dishwasher repair</a>. Full model coverage on the <a href="/services/dishwasher-repair/">dishwasher repair</a> hub. Nearby: <a href="/beverly-hills/dishwasher-repair/">Beverly Hills</a>, <a href="/pasadena/dishwasher-repair/">Pasadena</a>. <a href="/book/">Book online</a> or call {phone}.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 05 FAQ -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">05 · FAQ</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">GE dishwasher not draining: common questions.</h2>

    <div class="faq-list">
      {faqs.map(f => (
        <details class="faq-item">
